    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Brady Street’s historic district earned National Register status in 1990 in the city of Milwaukee.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Brady_Street_Historic_District"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The street’s first building, a 2‑story cream‑brick Italianate shop, dates to about 1875 and once housed three storefronts and living quarters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Brady_Street_Historic_District"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1930s Italian immigrants settled on Brady Street, turning it into a neighborhood known as Little Italy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Brady_Street_Historic_District"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 2004 Brady Street Bus Shelter, 2006 Marsupial Bridge, and 2012 Trestle Deck are modern public‑space projects that line the western end of the street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Brady_Street_Historic_District"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A 1921 storefront addition on Brady Street has hosted several plumbing contractors over the decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Brady_Street_Historic_District"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Brady Street hosts an annual festival featuring local bands, vendor booths, and activities for all ages, showcasing its lively spirit.",
